window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Feather In The Dust</b><br> <i>A heart-lifting tale of friendship, faith, and redemption that will stay with you long after the final tick.</i></p> <p>Elia is the kind of girl most people don’t notice—quiet, careful, invisible in the rush of everyday life. She keeps her head down at school, tiptoes through the silence at home, and clings to the memory of the one person who truly saw her: Grandpa.</p> <p>When he passes, all she has left is his worn Bible and the whispered promise that God sees her—even when no one else does.</p> <p>Then, one day in the woods, she finds something impossible: a fallen angel, hidden in the trees. Broken. Angry. Alone. His name is Azarel, and he wants nothing to do with the world—or with her. But Elia is stubborn. Gentle. Persistent in the way only someone full of quiet hope can be.</p> <p>As their unlikely friendship deepens, both begin to heal in ways they never expected. Through whispered prayers, crayon-written verses, and small acts of love, Elia shows Azarel a kind of grace he’s never known—and in doing so, discovers her own voice, strength, and purpose.</p> <p>Beautifully written and deeply moving, <i>Feather In The Dust</i> is a story about being seen, being loved, and learning that even the most broken among us are never beyond redemption. Perfect for fans of <i>The Shack</i>, <i>Bridge to Terabithia</i>, and <i>The Boy, the Mole, the Fox and the Horse</i>.</p>"; 
